Z||000003||thomas_l||12-11-2001||09:02 AM||||My dad has a 62 Impala that is set up for pro street rusting away in his garage. The interior and body are disassembled and there is LOTS to do. The rear is tubbed with a narrowed axle, 15 X 12's and slicks on the ends. A supposedly stock rebuilt 454 in the front ought to be OK. But it will likely rust a little more before it gets done. <P>The project that's ahead of the 62 will be slamming his 01 3500 Silverado dually with a 6/8 drop and all the goodies. Drop spindles up front, flip kit & air bags in back, delete the rear bumper for a roll pan & hidden hitch. We'll probably get enough black paint to do the roll pan and black out the chrome on the grille and side mirrors too. To top it off he's got a set of diamondback alloys that he plans to get chromed.<P>Meanwhile I just wrapped up a restore of a 94 Crown Vic police car in my own garage. Pretty boring in comparison  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> but it will fund a car trailer for me to haul broken Fieros on  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
